Di'Anno: Di'Anno was a band featuring former Iron Maiden singer Paul Di'Anno, whom the band was named after.

CSN (album): CSN is the third studio album by Crosby, Stills & Nash released in 1977.  It is the second release by the trio configuration and the first without Neil Young since his entry into the band.  It peaked at #2 on the "Billboard" Top Pop Albums chart; two singles taken from the album, Nash's "Just a Song Before I Go" and Stills' "Fair Game" peaked at #7 and #43 respectively on the "Billboard" Hot 100.  It is currently the trio configuration's best selling record, outselling 1969's "Crosby, Stills & Nash" by 200,000 copies.  It has been certified quadruple platinum by RIAA.

